# Normalise line endings so a clean clone actually runs.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true is common there) but
# every script runs inside WSL/Linux containers. Without the rules below, a
# fresh clone checks scripts out with CRLF and they fail immediately with:
#     bash: /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# which is a confusing way to discover a line-ending problem. Same class of
# breakage for YAML consumed by Docker Compose and for .env files read by
# containers.

# Adopted from HACKATHON_1/.gitattributes (maria/containerization): pinning
# eol=lf on the catch-all is more deterministic than bare `text=auto`, which
# lets each platform decide. Everything here is consumed by Linux containers,
# so LF is the right default and the exceptions below are the exceptions.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Must be LF regardless of platform -- these are executed by Linux.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.env           text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# PowerShell is Windows-only here; CRLF is the native convention for it.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Binary -- never touch.
*.pdf           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
